Prepare target and restoration files from the saved original Config. Each of the ten target fields must differ from its original value:
python3 - '<run-dir>' <<'PY'
import json, sys
from pathlib import Path
run = Path(sys.argv[1])
original = json.loads((run / 'config-original.json').read_text())
choices = {'temperatureUnit': ('f', 'c'), 'altitudeUnit': ('ft', 'm'), 'measurementInterval': (17, 19), 'gpsMode': ('always', 'off'), 'backLedBrightness': (2, 1), 'touchLedIntensity': (2, 1), 'buzzerEnabled': (False, True), 'co2AbcDays': (0, 1), 'tvocLearningOffset': (24, 12), 'noxLearningOffset': (24, 12)}
target = {k: b if original[k] == a else a for k, (a, b) in choices.items()}
restore = {k: original[k] for k in choices}
for name, value in [('config-target.json', target), ('config-restore.json', restore)]:
    (run / name).write_text(json.dumps(value, indent=2) + '\n')
print(json.dumps(target, indent=2))
PY

In a new case-specific directory, save this as provision.json, replacing credentials and all addresses with reserved values for the test LAN:
{
  "ssid": "TEST-SSID",
  "password": "TEST-PASSWORD",
  "disableCloud": true,
  "staticIp": {
    "ip": "192.168.1.220",
    "netmask": "255.255.255.0",
    "gateway": "192.168.1.1",
    "dns": "192.168.1.1"
  }
}
Submit: curl --max-time 5 -i -X POST http://192.168.4.1/api/provision -H 'Content-Type: application/json' --data-binary @provision.json
